// Read/write one grid cell. grid_set uses the generic lset "store into an
// imported list" idiom (see demos/gl3dgame/world/game/state/mutate.id):
// passing the imported list as a parameter makes it an assignable identifier
// again, and lists are reference-semantic so the store is shared.

grid_get(int x, int z) {
  int ret_i = (import mgrid)[z * (import grid_w) + x];
} return int ret_i;
given maze_init (0, 0):(1)
given maze_init (14, 12):(1)
given open_room_setup (1, 1):(0)

grid_set(int x, int z, int v) {
  int grid_index_v = z * (import grid_w) + x;
  lset((import mgrid), grid_index_v, v);
} return void;
given maze_init (3, 4, 0):() then grid_check_3_4:(0)
given maze_init (3, 4, 7):() then grid_check_3_4:(7)

// Test check: cell (3,4) read through a zero-argument wrapper, since a
// `then` check takes none but grid_get needs both coordinates.
grid_check_3_4() {
  int ret_i = grid_get(3, 4);
} return int ret_i;
given maze_init ():(1)
given maze_init ():(1) then calls grid_get:(3, 4)
